When a user cancels the workflow while `steps.release` is running, the job has no job-level condition and therefore uses `success()`. GitHub Actions cancels the job before it evaluates the later step. The step-level `always()` cannot override a cancelled job, so the gap report does not run. A partially published crate can therefore remain undetected.

